meta {
  name: Get Activity
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/activities/1
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  # Get Activity by ID

  Retrieves a specific activity by its ID.

  ## URL Parameters
  - `activity_id`: The ID of the activity to retrieve

  ## Response
  Returns full ActivityResponse object with all fields including:
  - Basic info (name, type, time, duration)
  - Location (address, coordinates)
  - Cost details
  - Booking information
  - Status and notes
  - Timestamps (created_at, updated_at as Unix timestamps)

  ## Access Control
  - Requires authentication
  - User must own the trip containing this activity's trip day
  - Returns 403 Forbidden if user doesn't own the trip
  - Returns 404 Not Found if activity doesn't exist

  ## Example Usage
  ```
  GET /api/v1/activities/5
  ```

  Response:
  ```json
  {
    "id": 5,
    "trip_day_id": 3,
    "name": "Meiji Shrine Visit",
    "activity_type": "cultural",
    "time": "09:00",
    "duration": 2.0,
    "location": "Meiji Shrine",
    "cost": 0.0,
    "currency": "JPY",
    "status": "planned",
    "created_at": 1704672000,
    "updated_at": 1704672000
  }
  ```
}
